        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "aa3372df-883f-50e7-b6c6-9c7dc7db4ee2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Ships: Celestyal Crystal, Louis Cristal, Leeward\n- Companies: Celestyal Cruises, Louis Cruise Lines, Louis Group, Norwegian Cruise Line, Norwegian Cruise Line Holdings Ltd.\n- Places: Cyprus, La Spezia, Italy, Bermuda, Miami-Dade County, Florida\n\nFacts:\n- In 1994, Celestyal Crystal partially sank.\n- After the 1994 sinking, Celestyal Crystal was rebuilt at Industrie Navali Maccaniche Affini in La Spezia, Italy.\n- After rebuilding, Celestyal Crystal re-entered service as MS Leeward for Norwegian Cruise Line.\n- Celestyal Crystal was previously named Louis Cristal.\n- Celestyal Crystal has been operated by the Cyprus-based Celestyal Cruises and previously by Louis Cruise Lines.\n- Celestyal Cruises and Louis Cruise Lines are both part of the Louis Group.\n- Norwegian Cruise Line Holdings Ltd. is a Bermudian company that operates cruise ships.\n- Norwegian Cruise Line Holdings Ltd. is headquartered in unincorporated Miami-Dade County, Florida.",
